      "division_name": "Chennai Division",
      "depot_name": "CGL Depot"
    },
    "initial_findings": "Found cracked nitrile O-ring on air manifold inlet pipe and a loose compression fitting on the secondary line, causing a slow audible leak during the charging cycle.\n\nThe pressure switch was also found chattering because of moisture in the sensing line.\n\nNo other abnormality was seen on the drive mechanism.",
    "action_taken": "Depressurized the cylinder, isolated the supply and removed the worn gasket.\n\nInstalled a new seal kit, replaced the compression fitting and drained the sensing line.\n\nLeak-tested at 15 bar for two hours with soap solution and a calibrated gauge.",
    "final_remarks": "Operating smoothly without pressure drop over 2 hours.\n\nBreaker closed and opened five times with normal charging time.\n\nAdvised the station staff to drain the air receiver every shift.",
